1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,714
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:02,764 --> 00:00:06,012
AI for Young Builders, video 10.

3
00:00:06,062 --> 00:00:10,650
How chatbots write: predicting the next word.

4
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:13,471
Chatbots seem to think.

5
00:00:13,521 --> 00:00:18,016
But at their heart they do one simple thing, over and over:

6
00:00:18,066 --> 00:00:19,710
predict the next word.

7
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:26,248
Give a language model the words: the cat sat on the.

8
00:00:26,298 --> 00:00:30,587
It gives every possible next word a chance.

9
00:00:30,637 --> 00:00:32,504
Mat is very likely.

10
00:00:32,554 --> 00:00:35,330
Floor and sofa are possible.

11
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:37,752
Banana is very unlikely.

12
00:00:37,802 --> 00:00:41,990
It picks one, adds it, and predicts again.

13
00:00:43,350 --> 00:00:45,638
Where do the chances come from?

14
00:00:45,688 --> 00:00:50,162
The model read a huge amount of text and learned which words

15
00:00:50,212 --> 00:00:51,746
tend to follow which.

16
00:00:51,796 --> 00:00:58,080
Big chatbots learned from billions of sentences, so their predictions are very good.

17
00:00:59,450 --> 00:01:04,383
In your lesson you will train a tiny model on one short story.

18
00:01:04,433 --> 00:01:09,446
Start it with the monsoon, and it writes a sentence using words

19
00:01:09,496 --> 00:01:10,651
from its story.

20
00:01:10,701 --> 00:01:14,830
It sounds sensible, but it has no idea what rain is.

21
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:18,223
Here is the big lesson.

22
00:01:18,273 --> 00:01:22,561
A language model picks words that sound likely.

23
00:01:22,611 --> 00:01:26,252
It does not check whether they are true.

24
00:01:26,302 --> 00:01:31,882
That is why chatbots sometimes invent facts, books or quotes.

25
00:01:31,932 --> 00:01:34,743
People call this hallucination.

26
00:01:34,793 --> 00:01:37,420
Always check important facts.

27
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:40,064
Let us recap.

28
00:01:40,114 --> 00:01:45,384
A language model predicts the next word, again and again.

29
00:01:45,434 --> 00:01:50,799
It learns which words follow which from its training text.

30
00:01:50,849 --> 00:01:55,093
Sounding likely is not the same as being true.

31
00:01:55,143 --> 00:01:58,080
Next: Talk to a real AI, safely.
